{"time": "2026-10-20T18:53:25.792373+03:00", "tool": "openalex_work", "args": [], "kwargs": {"work": "W2761960239"}, "response": {"provenance": {"source": "OpenAlex", "request": "https://api.openalex.org/works/W2761960239?", "retrieved": "2026-10-20", "untrusted_text_fields": ["title", "abstract", "description"]}, "work": {"openalex_id": "W2761960239", "title": "Observation of Quantum Interference in the Plasmonic Hong-Ou-Mandel Effect", "year": 2014, "authors": [{"name": "Giuliana Di Martino", "openalex_id": "A5080211452", "institutions": ["Imperial College London"]}, {"name": "Yannick Sonnefraud", "openalex_id": "A5089205104", "institutions": ["Centre National de la Recherche Scientifique", "Institut Néel"]}, {"name": "Mark Tame", "openalex_id": "A5038373641", "institutions": ["Imperial College London", "University of KwaZulu-Natal"]}, {"name": "Stéphane Kéna‐Cohen", "openalex_id": "A5024955035", "institutions": ["Polytechnique Montréal", "Imperial College London"]}, {"name": "Frederik Dieleman", "openalex_id": "A5016848010", "institutions": ["Imperial College London"]}, {"name": "Şahin Kaya Özdemir", "openalex_id": "A5016725403", "institutions": ["Washington University in St. Louis"]}, {"name": "M.S. Kim", "openalex_id": "A5068519759", "institutions": ["Imperial College London"]}, {"name": "Stefan Alexander Maier", "openalex_id": "A5009223920", "institutions": ["Imperial College London"]}], "source": "Physical Review Applied", "type": "article", "cited_by": 104, "doi": "10.1103/physrevapplied.1.034004", "oa_status": "green", "oa_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/1402.0813", "publication_date": "2014-04-15", "volume": "1", "issue": "3", "pages": null, "topic": {"name": "Plasmonic and Surface Plasmon Research", "field": "Engineering", "domain": "Physical Sciences"}, "references_count": 39, "is_retracted": false, "pdf_urls": ["https://arxiv.org/pdf/1402.0813"], "abstract": "Surface plasmon polaritons (SPPs) are electromagnetic excitations recently found to enable ultracompact quantum circuitry. For the first time, two indistinguishable SPPs are produced and made to interfere, demonstrating conclusively that they behave as bosons and opening up new opportunities for controlling quantum states."}}}
{"time": "2026-10-20T18:55:12.804801+03:00", "tool": "openalex_work", "args": [], "kwargs": {"work": "W2015275764"}, "response": {"provenance": {"source": "OpenAlex", "request": "https://api.openalex.org/works/W2015275764?", "retrieved": "2026-10-20", "untrusted_text_fields": ["title", "abstract", "description"]}, "work": {"openalex_id": "W2015275764", "title": "Multiphoton entanglement and interferometry", "year": 2012, "authors": [{"name": "Jian-Wei Pan", "openalex_id": "A5042449260", "institutions": ["University of Science and Technology of China"]}, {"name": "Zeng‐Bing Chen", "openalex_id": "A5060492935", "institutions": ["University of Science and Technology of China"]}, {"name": "Chao‐Yang Lu", "openalex_id": "A5032099658", "institutions": ["University of Science and Technology of China"]}, {"name": "Harald Weinfurter", "openalex_id": "A5043938679", "institutions": ["Max Planck Institute of Quantum Optics", "Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München"]}, {"name": "Anton Zeilinger", "openalex_id": "A5001105113", "institutions": ["University of Vienna", "Austrian Academy of Sciences"]}, {"name": "Marek Żukowski", "openalex_id": "A5036398885", "institutions": ["University of Science and Technology of China", "University of Vienna"]}], "source": "Reviews of Modern Physics", "type": "article", "cited_by": 1409, "doi": "10.1103/revmodphys.84.777", "oa_status": "green", "oa_url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0805.2853", "publication_date": "2012-05-11", "volume": "84", "issue": "2", "pages": "777–838", "topic": {"name": "Quantum Information and Cryptography", "field": "Computer Science", "domain": "Physical Sciences"}, "references_count": 553, "is_retracted": false, "pdf_urls": ["https://arxiv.org/pdf/0805.2853"], "abstract": "Multiphoton interference reveals strictly nonclassical phenomena. Its applications range from fundamental tests of quantum mechanics to photonic quantum information processing, where a significant fraction of key experiments achieved so far comes from multiphoton state manipulation. The progress, both theoretical and experimental, of this rapidly advancing research is reviewed. The emphasis is given to the creation of photonic entanglement of various forms, tests of the completeness of quantum mechanics (in particular, violations of local realism), quantum information protocols for quantum communication (e.g., quantum teleportation, entanglement purification, and quantum repeater), and quantum computation with linear optics. The scope of the review is limited to ``few-photon'' phenomena involving measurements of discrete observables."}}}
